","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2021-04-10T20:34:32Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/817204180","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1844#issuecomment-817204180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1844","id":817204180,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgxNzIwNDE4MA==","user":{"login":"TehPers","id":2214247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTQyNDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2214247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers","html_url":"https://github.com/TehPers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-10T21:24:14Z","updated_at":"2021-04-10T21:24:46Z","body":"I think that this could be solved using an attribute similar to serde's `#[serde(crate = \"...\")]` where you give the attribute (and thus the derive macro) the path to the `bevy_reflect` crate root. It might be worth noting that other bevy crates also have a `#[as_crate]` attribute (although I couldn't figure out the expected syntax for it).\r\n\r\nThe main issue I'm having with this crate vs. the other bevy crates is that this crate uses `crate` as the path to bevy_reflect when being re-exported whereas the other bevy crates use their respective crate names (`bevy_ecs`, `bevy_render`, etc). For example, to implement `Bundle`, I can do it like this:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n// Import the bevy_ecs crate as bevy_ecs\r\nuse foo::bevy::{ ecs as bevy_ecs, prelude::* };\r\n\r\n// implements bevy_ecs::bundle::Bundle\r\n#[derive(Bundle)]\r\nstruct MyBundle {\r\n    component: MyComponent,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I were instead to derive `TypeUuid`, it would attempt to implement `crate::TypeUuid` rather than `bevy_reflect::TypeUuid`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/817204180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"TehPers","id":2214247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTQyNDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2214247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers","html_url":"https://github.com/TehPers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TehPers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/817204745","html_url":"https://github.com/bevy